				\begin{document}$$ {s}_{ij}=\left({\sum}_j{t}_j/n\right)/\left(1000\cdot {t}_j\right) $$\end{document}sij=(∑jtj/n)/(1000⋅tj), where t
j is the total number of accessible peaks in cell j. (The 1000 in the denominator of the scale factor scales the measurements so that the f
ij are close to 1.)

We obtained the processed data from Rotem et al. [12], which consists of H3K4me2 ChIP-seq reads from 4587 cells, aggregated using 91 chromatin signatures. We found that these data required further normalization for the total sum of signature values per cell. We normalized the value of f
ij (signature i in cell j) by multiplying by the following scale factor: \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
