				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ P\left(Y\Big|\boldsymbol{t},{\sigma}^2,{\sigma}_{rbf}^2,l\right) = \mathcal{N}\left(Y\Big|0,{K}_{ff}+{\sigma}^2\boldsymbol{I}\right) $$\end{document}PY|t,σ2,σrbf2,l=NY|0,Kff+σ2I

where K
ff is the covariance matrix defined by the kernel function k. A simple approach to inferring the latent variable t would be to find the values that maximize the posterior distribution:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
